Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.34,0:00:07.39,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}翻译/压制/字幕制作：HAF半个水果
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.31,0:00:12.31,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(1940.893,388.557)}使用AI工具翻译，如有不准确的地方请在弹幕或评论区指正，谢谢！
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.34,0:00:17.34,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(1940.893,388.557)}翻译质量权威评价：原来25年就有小拉即用机翻糊弄人了
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.59,0:00:13.01,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Hello everybody. So in this video I'll show you how I ran Linux on Microsoft Excel.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.70,0:00:17.97,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Microsoft Excel is a very powerful suit and you can do lots of things in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.25,0:00:19.71,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Accountants love it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.98,0:00:22.16,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Software engineering students despise it
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.19,0:00:25.25,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,because universities hate their software engineering students
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.48,0:00:27.30,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and force them to do Excel assignments.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.59,0:00:28.54,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,True story.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.92,0:00:32.79,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,But anyway, enthusiasts do all sorts of freaky stuff in Excel,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.24,0:00:36.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and this project is just an excuse for me to make a funny video.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.49,0:00:40.26,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Originally, NSG 650 made that thing,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.47,0:00:44.93,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and he tweeted about it. I got pretty excited, so I contacted him about it,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.95,0:00:47.21,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and he then published the source code.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.75,0:00:52.33,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, upon closer inspection, I realized his version was pretty bare bones,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.60,0:00:54.10,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,only printing the output.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.33,0:00:56.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,And I thought it'd make a pretty lame video.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.10,0:01:02.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs104}So ultimately, I decided to chip in and sort of finish the project for him, making it interactive.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.17,0:01:06.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Took me a couple hours, but I'm pretty happy with how it turned out.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.80,0:01:09.65,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I don't want to take long. So, let's just see it in action.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.99,0:01:11.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,And then I'll explain how it works.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.59,0:01:16.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,All right. So, to run it, it's simple enough. Just open the Excel spreadsheet.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.22,0:01:21.45,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,It's not an ordinary spreadsheet, as you can probably tell by the file name already.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.75,0:01:23.86,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,It's a spreadsheet full of macros.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.57,0:01:29.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I can smell your fear. Don't worry, there is no macro virus in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.83,0:01:31.55,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,These times are long over
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.17,0:01:35.13,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Though you should probably keep an eye out just in case.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.67,0:01:39.02,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,So, you open that file and wow,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.04,0:01:42.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,this is Linux running in Microsoft Excel.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.55,0:01:45.76,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Unbelievable. Let me make this a little
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.76,0:01:48.27,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,more viewable by scaling the interface up.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.95,0:01:53.37,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,There we go. If the screen overflows, it just resets the A column.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.56,0:01:59.94,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs81}so this is the reason there isn't all that extra boot information at the beginning we used to have when it wasn't scaled up.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.86,0:02:04.67,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,The rules are simple. There are no rules. It's Linux.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.50,0:02:09.57,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,But jokes aside, the entire A column is reserved for the terminal output.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.88,0:02:13.33,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,But where do you run the Linux commands? Good question.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.58,0:02:17.50,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I reserved the C2 cell specifically for the terminal input.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.88,0:02:19.06,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,That's where you run them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.61,0:02:22.68,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,You can do all the terminal basics in that powershell.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.35,0:02:25.26,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,run the directory listing
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.68,0:02:27.11,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,switch the directories
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.68,0:02:28.99,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,create files
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:32.45,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,even enter and exit Vim.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.61,0:02:38.10,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,The only critical mistake you can make is entering the insert mode in Vim.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.83,0:02:42.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Naturally, you'd need to press escape to get back out
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.46,0:02:45.82,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but there is so far no way to input that in the cell.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.30,0:02:50.59,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I mean, you can technically create magic sequences that translate to special keys
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.97,0:02:52.98,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but I didn't bother to implement that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.53,0:02:56.56,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,It's a simple switch case statement in the handler function.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.05,0:02:59.47,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,But anyway, you can even run scripts,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.70,0:03:01.75,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,even though I kind of failed to do that,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.13,0:03:05.94,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I think, because I couldn't input the new line after the shebang.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.55,0:03:08.88,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,So, it's still pretty raw.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.43,0:03:11.30,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,There are lots of things you can do,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.63,0:03:15.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs104}but from here on out, it's just tedious work of implementing different magic sequences,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.99,0:03:21.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,essentially converting input from an Excel cell to the Linux std in.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.99,0:03:23.59,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Not a fan of tedious work.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.22,0:03:31.17,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs90}Anyway, let's just say I tried to run devil fetch even though it's a bash script and there is no bash here.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.63,0:03:32.72,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Hope dies last.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.80,0:03:35.44,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Spoiler, it did not work.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.85,0:03:39.64,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,And moreover, it crashed the macro a couple times I tried.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.54,0:03:45.82,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs104}I guess the coolest tedious thing you can implement is the ASI escape sequences support
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.06,0:03:48.18,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so that you could beautify the output.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.86,0:03:51.46,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,But again, it's pretty annoying to implement.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.39,0:03:55.61,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,So yeah, this is Linux running in Microsoft Excel.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.43,0:03:57.78,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,What's the catch?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.13,0:04:04.40,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs104}Well, you could consider it cheating because it's not Linux running in native Excel formulas.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.10,0:04:08.60,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,If you do want to implement Linux in pure Excel formulas,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.41,0:04:11.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry for you, my friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.61,0:04:17.78,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs104}But be my guest. In reality, Linux is running in a separate library that's loaded into Excel
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.81,0:04:24.38,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,via the VBA macro. Excel here basically acts as the IO interface.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.01,0:04:28.55,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,The library we're using is mini RV32
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.96,0:04:33.50,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,which is the tiniest risk V emulator that fits inside a C header.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.16,0:04:40.58,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs100}I don't really want to go in depth into the technicalities neither of the VBA macro nor the library.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.22,0:04:43.31,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'll try to explain in simple terms.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.69,0:04:49.24,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Basically, an emulator allows you to step tick by tick with a function.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.66,0:04:52.61,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,And each tick there is an event loop that's running.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.14,0:04:56.54,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Every tick, essentially a moment in time you choose
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.87,0:05:00.82,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,you get to send input into the emulator and receive output from it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.21,0:05:06.82,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,The VBA macro runs 2 to the power of 17 ticks in the emulator at the very beginning
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.82,0:05:08.80,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and every time input is received.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.80,0:05:13.11,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I just picked that number because I think number 17 is cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.74,0:05:17.89,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,And it was somewhat the golden middle between the macro freezing Excel entirely
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.41,0:05:23.48,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs98}and having enough time for theemulator to run an average command and return the output from it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.20,0:05:27.10,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,So that's how the VBA script works essentially
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.77,0:05:31.08,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,the library is a little more tricky to explain in simple terms
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.57,0:05:33.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,but the event loop is located in it
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.97,0:05:38.04,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,and the CSR read and write functions are invoked every tick.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.91,0:05:43.70,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs104}So we get to process input and send the output with the functions exported from the DLL.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.11,0:05:47.28,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,They're then imported and used accordingly in the VBA script.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.02,0:05:49.78,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,It's just an orchestra really.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.66,0:05:55.96,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs95}That's one of the more weird and satisfying projects I have worked on since the start of my channel.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.37,0:06:00.42,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I can't thank NSG650 enough for sharing the initial source code.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.45,0:06:02.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,This wouldn't have been possible without him.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.30,0:06:05.20,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,He's a cool guy. Check him out.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.58,0:06:11.34,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs80}I'm going to leave both the source code and the compiled library along with a micro sheet in the description below
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.62,0:06:13.42,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,so you can try it out for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.78,0:06:16.91,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Tweet the coolest stuff you can execute in that spreadsheet at me
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.41,0:06:19.47,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm Andderman on Twitter.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.65,0:06:23.29,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'll retweet the craziest stuff you guys execute.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.89,0:06:28.21,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,{\fs104}I believe collectively you can do much more than me in such a stripped down Linux version.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.75,0:06:31.32,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,And I'm sorry if my voice is kind of annoying right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.58,0:06:34.52,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm currently sick and my nose is stuffed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.10,0:06:38.05,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,I'm trying my best to voice things over right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.76,0:06:40.79,Enderman-EN,,0,0,0,,Thanks for watching and take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.59,0:00:13.01,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,大家好。在这个视频中，我将向大家展示如何在Microsoft Excel上运行Linux
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.70,0:00:17.97,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,Microsoft Excel是一款功能非常强大的软件，你可以在其中完成许多任务
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.25,0:00:19.71,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,会计师们很喜欢它
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.98,0:00:22.16,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,软件工程专业的学生对它深恶痛绝
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.19,0:00:25.25,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,因为大学讨厌他们的软件工程专业学生
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.48,0:00:27.30,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,还强迫他们做Excel作业
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.59,0:00:28.54,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,真事
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.92,0:00:32.79,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但不管怎样，爱好者们在Excel里总能玩出各种疯狂的花样
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.24,0:00:36.88,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,而这个项目只是我为了拍个有趣的视频找的借口
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.49,0:00:40.26,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,最初，NSG650制作了这个东西
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.47,0:00:44.93,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,他还在推特上发了相关内容。我对此感到非常兴奋，于是联系了他
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.95,0:00:47.21,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,然后他公布了源代码
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.75,0:00:52.33,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,遗憾的是，经过仔细检查后，我发现他的版本相当简陋
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.60,0:00:54.10,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,只有打印输出
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.33,0:00:56.86,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我还以为这视频会拍得很无聊
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.10,0:01:02.48,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,最终，我决定插手帮忙，算是替他完成了这个项目，还让它具备了互动性
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.17,0:01:06.24,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,花了我几个小时，但对最终的效果相当满意
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.80,0:01:09.65,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我不想说太多。直接看实际操作吧
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.99,0:01:11.88,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,然后我会解释它是如何工作的
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.59,0:01:16.86,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,好的。那么，运行它很简单。只需打开Excel电子表格即可
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.22,0:01:21.45,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这不是一份普通的电子表格，从文件名你大概就能看出来
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.75,0:01:23.86,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这是一张满是宏的电子表格
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.57,0:01:29.48,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我能闻到你恐惧的气息。别担心，这里没有宏病毒
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.83,0:01:31.55,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,那样的日子早已一去不复返
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.17,0:01:35.13,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,不过以防万一，你最好还是留意一下
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.67,0:01:39.02,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,好了，你打开文件，哇
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.04,0:01:42.20,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这是在Microsoft Excel中运行的Linux
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.55,0:01:45.76,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,难以置信。让我把界面
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.76,0:01:48.27,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,放大一点，这样看起来更清楚
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.95,0:01:53.37,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,好了。如果屏幕溢出，它就会重置A列
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.56,0:01:59.94,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这就是为什么启动时没有看到所有那些额外引导信息了
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.86,0:02:04.67,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,规则很简单。没有规则。这就是Linux
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.50,0:02:09.57,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,玩笑归玩笑，整个A列是专门留给终端输出的
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.88,0:02:13.33,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但在哪里运行这些Linux命令呢？问得好
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.58,0:02:17.50,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我特意为终端输入保留了C2单元格
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.88,0:02:19.06,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,那就是你运行它们的地方
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.61,0:02:22.68,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,你可以在那个PowerShell中完成所有终端基础操作
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.35,0:02:25.26,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,列举目录
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.68,0:02:27.11,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,切换目录
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.68,0:02:28.99,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,创建文件
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.00,0:02:32.45,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,甚至可以进入和退出 Vim
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.61,0:02:38.10,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,在Vim中，唯一可能犯的致命错误就是进入插入模式
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.83,0:02:42.08,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,当然，你需要按Esc键才能返回
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.46,0:02:45.82,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但目前还没有办法在单元格中输入这个
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.30,0:02:50.59,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我是说，从技术上讲，你可以创建映射到特殊键的魔法序列
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.97,0:02:52.98,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但我懒得去实现
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.53,0:02:56.56,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这是处理函数中的一个简单switch case语句
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.05,0:02:59.47,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但不管怎样，你甚至可以运行脚本
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.70,0:03:01.75,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,尽管我在这方面有些失败了
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.13,0:03:05.94,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我想，是因为我无法在单元格后面换行
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.55,0:03:08.88,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,所以，它还相当简陋
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.43,0:03:11.30,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,有许多事情你可以做
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.63,0:03:15.96,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但从现在开始，就只剩下实现各种魔法序列的繁琐工作了
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.99,0:03:21.40,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,本质上将Excel单元格的输入转换为Linux的标准输入
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.99,0:03:23.59,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,不喜欢繁琐的工作
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.22,0:03:31.17,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,不管怎样，就说我试图运行devil fetch吧，尽管这是个bash脚本而这里根本没有bash环境
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.63,0:03:32.72,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,希望最后才会破灭
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.80,0:03:35.44,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,剧透一下，这没有用
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.85,0:03:39.64,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,而且，我试了几次，它还导致宏崩溃了几次
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.54,0:03:45.82,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我猜你能实现的最酷又繁琐的功能就是支持ASI转义序列
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.06,0:03:48.18,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这样你就可以美化输出结果
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.86,0:03:51.46,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但话说回来，实现起来还是挺烦人的
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.39,0:03:55.61,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,没错，这就是在Microsoft Excel里运行的Linux
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.43,0:03:57.78,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,有什么猫腻？
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.13,0:04:04.40,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,嗯，你可以认为这是作弊，因为它并不是在原生Excel公式中运行的Linux
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.10,0:04:08.60,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,如果你确实想在纯Excel公式中实现Linux
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.41,0:04:11.28,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我很抱歉无法实现，我的朋友
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.61,0:04:17.78,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但请随意。实际上，Linux运行在一个独立的库中
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.81,0:04:24.38,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,该库通过VBA宏加载到Excel中。这里的Excel基本上充当了输入输出接口的角色
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.01,0:04:28.55,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我们使用的库是mini RV32
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.96,0:04:33.50,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这是能塞进C语言头文件的最小RISC-V模拟器
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.16,0:04:40.58,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我既不想深入探讨VBA宏的技术细节，也不想讨论这个库的技术问题
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.22,0:04:43.31,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我会尽量用简单的语言来解释
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.69,0:04:49.24,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,基本上，模拟器允许你通过一个函数逐步执行每个时钟周期
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.66,0:04:52.61,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,每个时钟周期都有一个正在运行的事件循环
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.14,0:04:56.54,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,每一个时刻，本质上是你选择的一个时间点
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.87,0:05:00.82,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,你可以向模拟器发送输入并接收其输出
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.21,0:05:06.82,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,VBA宏在模拟器中最初运行时以及每次接收到输入时，会运行2的17次方个时钟周期
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.82,0:05:08.80,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,VBA宏在模拟器中最初运行时以及每次接收到输入时，会运行2的17次方个时钟周期
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.80,0:05:13.11,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我选那个数字只是因为我觉得17很酷
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.74,0:05:17.89,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这大致是在宏完全冻结Excel与给予模拟器足够时间
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.41,0:05:23.48,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,运行平均命令并返回输出之间的一个理想折中点
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.20,0:05:27.10,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这就是VBA脚本的基本工作原理
Dialogue: 0,0:05:27.77,0:05:31.08,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,用简单的语言来解释这个库有点复杂
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.57,0:05:33.52,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但事件循环位于其中
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.97,0:05:38.04,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,每个时钟周期都会调用CSR的读写函数
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.91,0:05:43.70,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,因此我们可以处理输入并通过从DLL导出的函数发送输出
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.11,0:05:47.28,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,随后它们被导入并在VBA脚本中相应使用
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.02,0:05:49.78,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这不过是个协调分工的过程
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.66,0:05:55.96,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这是我频道创立以来做过的最古怪又最令人满足的项目之一
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.37,0:06:00.42,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我无法充分感谢NSG650分享最初的源代码
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.45,0:06:02.52,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,但没有他，这一切都不可能实现
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.30,0:06:05.20,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,他是个很酷的家伙。去关注他吧
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.58,0:06:11.34,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我将在下面的描述中同时提供源代码、编译好的库以及一份简要说明
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.62,0:06:13.42,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,这样你就可以亲自尝试一下
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.78,0:06:16.91,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,把你能在那个电子表格里执行的最酷的东西发推给我
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.41,0:06:19.47,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我推特是endermanch
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.65,0:06:23.29,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我会转发你们执行的那些最疯狂的事情
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.89,0:06:28.21,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我相信在这个精简版的Linux系统中，你们集体能做的远比我一个人多
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.75,0:06:31.32,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,如果我现在的声音有点烦人，我很抱歉
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.58,0:06:34.52,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我现在生病了，有点鼻塞
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.10,0:06:38.05,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,我正在尽力为当前的内容配音
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.76,0:06:40.79,Enderman-CN,,0,0,0,,感谢观看，保重
